BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Shorenstein Asia-Pacific Research Center (APARC)] In the Global V
 anguard: Agrarian Development and the Making of Modern Taiwan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T131500
DTSTAMP:20261101T181711Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54066223932423-54066223933448@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In just half a century\, Taiwan transformed from an agricultur
 al colony into an economic power\, spurred by efforts of the authoritarian
  Republic of China government in land reform\, farmers associations\, and 
 improved crop varieties. Yet overlooked is how Taiwan brought these practi
 ces to the developing world. In the Global Vanguard elucidates the history
  and impact of the “Taiwan model” of agrarian development by incorpora
 ting how Taiwanese experts took the country’s agrarian success and expor
 ted\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://aparc.fsi.stanford.edu/events/globa
 l-vanguard-agrarian-development-and-making-modern-taiwan\nLast synced: 202
 6-11-01 10:17 PST
LOCATION:Encina Hall
URL:https://aparc.fsi.stanford.edu/events/global-vanguard-agrarian-develop
 ment-and-making-modern-taiwan
END:VEVENT
