SUMMARY:[Stanford Humanities Center] Policed: A Latinx History of State Vi
 olence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T133000
DTSTAMP:20261101T181711Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54287265783171-54287265784196@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Spanning the nineteenth century to the present\, Policed: A La
 tinx History of State Violence\, examines how policing became a key compon
 ent in the formation of Latinx identity and political consciousness\, and 
 still lies at the heart of many pressing issues confronting Latinx communi
 ties today\, including immigration\, employment\, health\, and housing. Mo
 re than simply telling a story of police brutality and harassment\, Mariso
 l LeBrón powerfully shows that Latinx people have continually resisted st
 ate\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-01 10:17 PST
LOCATION:Humanities Center
END:VEVENT
