DTSTAMP:20261101T181711Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54357712150615-54357712151640@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract\n\nLithium-bearing brines offer the United States an 
 opportunity to co-produce critical minerals and geothermal energy. Realizi
 ng this potential requires a better understanding of brine chemistry\, res
 ervoir dynamics\, and the long-term sustainability of lithium extraction.
 \n\nThe Salton Sea geothermal field in California is a distinctive setting
  for lithium–geothermal co-production. Since 2004\, geothermal brine pro
 duction has averaged just over 120 million metric tons per year. At an est
 imat\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-11-01 10:17 PST
LOCATION:Green Earth Sciences Building
END:VEVENT
