 sification events in the history of life on our planet: the Cambrian Explo
 sion (~530 to 510 Ma) and the Great Ordovician Biodiversification Event (~
 471 to 458 Ma)\, or GOBE. These two events are separated by a plateau dive
 rsity that spanned from the later Cambrian and Early Ordovician\, roughly 
 ~40 million years. On a finer temporal scale\, the fossil record shows tha
 t this diversity plateau contains at least six rapid turnover events in\n
